    "title": "WATCH: Tornado Warning active in multiple Central New York counties - NewsBreak",
    "text": "2 hours ago\nWatch the live stream of NewsChannel 9 Chief Metrologist Jim Teske's severe weather coverage above.\nSYRACUSE, N.Y. -- A Tornado Warning has been issued for three counties in Central New York.\nThe National Weather Service in Binghamton has issued a Tornado Warning for Northwestern Cayuga County Northwestern Seneca County, Onondaga County, Chenango County and Madison County on Wednesday night, Sept. 2. Onondaga County's warning is the most recent, issued around 9:05 p.m.\nPeople are urged to be in the lowest part of the home they are currently in, preferably with no windows. Stay away from exterior walls.\nThe service noted flying debris will be dangerous to people without shelter, with damage to roof, vehicles and vehicles and likely tree damage.\nA Tornado Watch was issued for Central New York earlier in the day. Chemung, Schuyler, Seneca Tompkins and Yates counites are under severe thunderstorm warnings.\nLatest Stories Latest Stories WATCH: Tornado Warning active in multiple Central New York counties UPDATE: Tornado Watch issued for Central New York Townline Road reopens after months of repairs; long-term maintenance debate continues Woman dies in crash on I-81 near Tully, state police investigating New York State Fair to close early as storms approach Syracuse area Copyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WSYR.",
    "summary": "Watch the live stream of NewsChannel 9 Chief Metrologist Jim Teske's severe weather coverage above. Onondaga County's warning is the most recent, issued around 9:05 p.m. People are urged to be in the lowest part of the home they are currently in, preferably with no windows. Chemung, Schuyler, Seneca Tompkins and Yates counites are under severe thunderstorm warnings.",
